import Foundation

/// One version in What's new.
public struct Release: Sendable, Equatable {
    public let version: String
    public let date: String
    public let items: [String]
}

/// The words of Settings: What's new (every version, newest first) and How it works.
public enum AppText {
    public static let releases: [Release] = [
        Release(version: "1.33", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: typing the weight and the reps on the machine page. Before, the keyboard opened only when you tapped exactly on the digits, which was easy to miss. Now a tap anywhere on the number area between the minus and the plus opens the keyboard, and the whole number is selected, so what you type replaces it (for example 32,5). A comma or a point both work. Done on the keyboard closes it. It is the same for seconds, minutes, level and incline on machines for time. Minus and plus work as before.",
            "New: type the weight during the rest. Under the rest ring the weight (1.31 had only minus and plus) is now a box you can tap and type in, with minus and plus beside it as before. A weight of 0 (body weight) now reads \"0 kg\" (before: \"Body\").",
            "New: a Reps row during the rest. Under the weight there is now a pale blue row \"Reps\" with a minus button, the reps and a plus button. It changes the reps of the next set at once, and the \"Next: set\" line follows. Type the number or use minus and plus (1 rep each). Before, the reps could not be changed during the rest: you had to tap Skip rest first. It shows on machines with weight and on exercises without a machine, not on machines for time.",
            "Changed: Change a set (tap a set you did). Before, Reps had only minus and plus. Now Reps is a box you can type in, with minus and plus beside it.",
            "Changed: the Next time form (\"How did it feel? Next time…\"). Before, Weight and Reps had only minus and plus. Now both are boxes you can type in, with minus and plus beside them.",
            "Fixed: sliding a finger sideways took you back by accident. Before, a finger moving sideways while you tapped or double-tapped the weight (from the edge of the screen, or since iOS 26 from anywhere on the page) could take you back to the gym page. Now there is no swipe back: you leave a page only with the Back button at the top left or with the button at the bottom. This is so on the machine page, the gym page, History and Settings.",
            "Changed: the gym colour is now blue (build 2, his ask). Before, the At the gym card on Workouts, the gym name button, the Choose gym plate, Set done, the minus and plus buttons and the headings of the gym pages were indigo (#4f46e5, a purple-blue). Now they are the same blue as the round + on Workouts (#2f6fe0 by day, a lighter blue by night). The name band under the machine photos is a deep navy instead of deep indigo.",
            "Changed: Back to gym and Exercise done at the bottom of the machine page now look different from Set done (build 2, his ask). Before, both were the same full indigo. Now Set done is full green with white words, the positive step, and the bottom button is pale blue with blue words.",
            "Changed: the three buttons under the rest ring now have a light colour each (build 3, his ask). Before, −15 s and +15 s were white with dark words and Skip rest was full indigo. Now −15 s is pale yellow with amber words, +15 s pale orange with orange words, and Skip rest pale green with green words and a green mark. They work as before.",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.32", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "New: a guided stretch timer with voice cues, so you can stretch with your AirPods in and your eyes closed. For each stretch it runs in turns. GET READY, 8 seconds, orange: the voice says, for example, \"First one: Standing calf stretch. 30 seconds each side. Get into position.\" (\"Next one\" and \"Last one\" for the others), then counts Three, Two, One. HOLD, green: \"Hold. First side.\", with \"Halfway\", \"Ten seconds\" and Three, Two, One at the end. For a stretch done on each side: SWITCH SIDES, 5 seconds, indigo (\"Switch sides.\"), then HOLD again for the second side (\"Hold. Second side.\"). At the very end the voice says \"Stretch done. Well done.\" and a done page with Close appears; the session goes into History just like a list you ticked off.",
            "New: how long each hold lasts comes from the stretch's amount. \"30 s each side\" means 30 seconds on two sides, \"60 s\" or \"1 min\" means 60 seconds, and a stretch with no time counts as 30 seconds.",
            "New: the timer screen shows a big ring with the seconds left, a pill with the phase (Get ready, Hold, Switch sides), the stretch's name, its steps and where you feel it, \"Then: …\" with what comes next, a top line such as \"Stretch 2 of 6 · 4:10 left\" with a progress bar, and a small headphones mark. Controls: previous stretch, a big Pause button (the voice says \"Paused\" and \"Go on\") and next stretch; Close is at the top left. The screen stays on. The voice plays in your AirPods when they are connected (otherwise from the speaker), on top of your music, and also when the silent switch is on.",
            "Changed: \"Stretch now\" on the Well done page now starts the timer, with the line \"Timer with voice cues in your AirPods\" under it. Before, it opened the list to tick off by hand.",
            "New: any exercise list whose exercises have times gets a full-colour \"Start the timer\" button at the top, with \"Voice cues in your AirPods\" under it. It shows until you tick the first exercise. This includes your own lists and the ready-made stretch lists.",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.31", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "New: change the weight during the rest. Under the rest ring, below the line \"Next: set 3 · …\", there is now a pale indigo row \"Weight\" with a minus button, the weight (for example \"34,5 kg\") and a plus button. Each tap moves the weight by the machine's own weight step, and a weight of 0 reads \"Body\". It changes the weight of the next set at once, and the \"Next: set\" line follows. Before, the weight could not be changed during the rest: you had to tap Skip rest first. The row shows only on machines where you log weight, not on reps-only exercises and not on machines for time.",
            "New: a session clock on the machine page. At the top left there is a small green pill with a softly pulsing dot and the session time (for example \"0:42:15\"), counting each second. It is the same clock as the green Session going line on the gym screen. When the clock is paused (20 minutes without a set) the pill turns grey and the dot stands still. Before, the machine page showed no session time and the top left was empty.",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.30", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: Plan today and Repeat last visit are now both green and look the same. Before, Plan today was plain indigo words on a pale indigo row, and Repeat last visit was a full indigo tile that stood out as the main one. Now they are two equal pale green tiles side by side, each with a green mark and green words. The green is the same as the \"Session going\" line (a deep green by day, a light green by night). They work exactly as before.",
            "Changed: the gym name button at the top of the gym screen. Before, it was a small indigo capsule only as wide as the gym's name. Now it is as wide as the card and as tall as the Plan today and Repeat last visit tiles (50 points): the gym's name on the left, a small arrow pointing down on the right, full indigo. Tap it and the Choose gym plate opens, as before.",
            "Changed: the opening hours line (\"Open until 22:00\", \"Closed · opens 06:00\" and so on) now sits under the gym name button. Before, it sat beside the capsule.",
            "Changed: Save as template has left the top of the gym screen. Before, it was a third tile beside Plan today and Repeat last visit, and it saved the machines of your LAST visit. Now the top has two tiles only, and saving a template is part of finishing a session.",
            "New: after Finish this session and End session, the \"Well done\" summary has a \"Save as template\" button. Tap it and give a name (for example \"Leg day\"); it keeps THIS session's machines, in the order you used them, as a plan template for this gym. Only machines with at least one set count, each once, and machines you have deleted are left out. Saving with a name that already exists in this gym replaces the old one. Afterwards the button says \"Saved as template · Leg day\" and shows a check mark. Cancel closes the name box and saves nothing.",
            "New: you find the template later under Plan today, in \"Use a template\". Saving a plan as a template inside Plan today works as before, and so does deleting templates in Settings → Plan templates.",
            "Changed: Earlier visits on the gym screen are now folded away. Before, the whole list always showed at the bottom of the screen under the heading \"Earlier visits · Basic-Fit\". Now there is one card with a small clock mark, the title \"Earlier visits\" and a line such as \"12 sessions at Basic-Fit · last Mon 16 Nov\", with an arrow at the right that turns when it is open. Tap the card to show the list, tap again to hide it. The rows are as before (newest first, tap one to open it). The card is closed each time you open the gym screen, so the machines stay close to the top.",
            "New: Discard session. The box \"End this session?\" (it opens from the red End on the green session line, and from Finish this session) now has a third button, a red \"Discard session\", shown once the session has at least one set. Before, the box had only \"End session\" and \"Continue the session\". Tapping it asks once more: \"Discard this session?\" — \"All 7 sets of this session are deleted. It will not show in Earlier visits or History. This cannot be undone.\" — with the buttons \"Discard session\" and \"Keep the session\". Discarding deletes the session and all its sets, stops the clock and clears that day's Busy marks and plan, like Finish does, but shows no Well done summary. Use it when you started by mistake.",
            "New: Discard on the \"Well done\" page. At the left of the bottom bar, beside Undo Finish and Done, there is now a red \"Discard\" button. Before, the bar had only Undo Finish and Done. It asks \"Discard this session?\": all its sets, the title, the notes and the photos are deleted, it will not show in Earlier visits or History, and it cannot be undone. \"Discard session\" does it; \"Keep the session\" leaves everything as it was.",
            "New: six ready-made stretch lists. Before, Settings → Reminder and stretch offered only the app's own After-gym stretch, your own exercise lists and None. Now it offers After-gym stretch plus six more, each with a one-line summary under its name: Legs after leg day (calves, thighs and hips), Upper body after push and pull (chest, back, arms and wrists), Lower back and hips, Neck and shoulders, Quick 3 minutes (4 stretches, when you are short of time) and After cardio (after treadmill, bike or rower). Your own lists and None are still there. A ready-made list you choose becomes an exercise list under Workouts the first time it is saved, and from then on it is yours to change.",
            "New: a Stretch guide page. At the top is a short how-to: hold still, no bouncing, a gentle pull and never pain, breathe, and do both sides. Then each stretch is numbered with its time, three to five steps, \"Where you feel it\" in green and \"Careful\" in orange. For your own stretches the page shows your note. Open it from Settings → Reminder and stretch → \"How to do these stretches\", or from the Well done page under Stretch now → \"How to do the stretches\".",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.29", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the gym chooser. Before, tapping the indigo pill with the gym's name at the top of the gym screen opened a plain pull-down menu: a see-through panel of text rows with no pictures, one row per gym (the one in use marked \"— here now\", a long name such as \"Basic-Fit Benalmadena\" wrapping onto two lines), then \"New gym…\", \"Log an earlier day…\", \"Rename this gym…\" and \"Opening hours…\". Now the pill slides a plate up from the bottom of the screen, about 60 percent of the screen tall, with a small grabber at the top; you can pull it up to full height. The pill itself is as it was: full indigo, the gym's name and a small arrow.",
            "New: the plate is headed \"Choose gym\", large and in the middle. Each gym is its own rounded row with a small hand-drawn gym mark in a pale indigo square and the gym's name on one line (a long name shrinks a little instead of wrapping). Under the name, only when opening hours are set, the open-now line (for example \"Open until 22:00\"). The gym you are in has an indigo outline, a small green \"Here now\" label and a filled indigo circle with a white tick; the others have a thin grey outline and an empty circle. Tap a gym to switch to it; the plate closes by itself.",
            "New: four buttons under the gyms, two rows of two, pale indigo with a hand-drawn picture above the word: \"New gym\" (a plus), \"Rename this gym\" (a pen), \"Opening hours\" (a clock) and \"Log an earlier day\" (a calendar). Each closes the plate and then opens what it opened before: the name box, the opening hours page or the day picker. Nothing about those changed. The clock and the calendar are two new small hand-drawn marks.",
            "New: a photo of each gym (your idea). The square at the left of a gym's row shows a small photo of the actual gym, 48 by 48 points. A gym without a photo shows the gym mark with a small camera at its corner. Tap the square to take a photo, choose one from Photos, or remove it. The photo is kept with your other photos and goes into your backups.",
            "New: a full indigo \"Done\" button at the bottom of the plate closes it without changing anything (on the Mac, the Escape key does the same).",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.28", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the first tab in the bar at the bottom is now called \"Workouts\". Before, it was called \"Train\". It is the same page with the same kettlebell mark, and its big heading is still \"Workout Companion\". The other two tabs, History and Settings, are as they were.",
            "Changed: the marks on each workout panel are bigger. The workout's icon at the top left grew from 30 to 42 points. The pen at the top right grew from 17 to 24 points, and its touch area is now 44 by 44 points. The round play button at the bottom right grew from a 28-point circle with a 13-point play mark to a 44-point circle with a 20-point play mark. The panel itself is a little taller: at least 148 points high, before 128.",
            "Changed: a tap on a workout panel now does three separate things. Before, tapping anywhere on the panel started the workout at once, and the play mark was only a picture. Now: tapping the panel shows the plan; tapping the pen opens the editor, as before; tapping the round play button starts the workout. Pressing and holding the panel still gives Edit, Duplicate and Delete. For VoiceOver, the panel now reads the name and the summary (before, it began with \"Start\"), and the play button says \"Start\" and the workout's name.",
            "New: the plan page. Tapping a workout panel opens a page you can read but not change. Nothing starts there and nothing can be edited. It is closed with \"Done\" (on the Mac, the Escape key closes it too). At the top it shows the workout's icon, its name and its kind (\"Sets & reps\", \"Exercise list\" or \"Interval timer\") on the workout's own colour. Under it, a Sets & reps workout lists \"Sets\" (for example 5), \"Reps each set\" (for example 20) and \"Rest between sets\" (for example 1:30, or \"None\" when the rest is 0). An Interval timer lists \"Rounds\", \"Work\", \"Rest\" (or \"None\") and \"Total time\". An Exercise list shows every exercise in order with its number, name, amount, note and photo, or \"No exercises yet\" when there is none.",
            "Changed: the + for a new workout moved to the bottom right. Before, it was a small + at the top right, where it cut into the heading \"Workout Companion\". Now it is a round blue button with a white +, 56 points wide, at the bottom right above the bar, in reach of your thumb.",
            "Removed: the dashed \"New workout\" tile after your workouts. Before, there were two ways to make a new workout (the tile and the +). Now there is one: the round + at the bottom right.",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.27", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the second line of the big \"At the gym\" card on Train. Before, when nothing was logged today and no opening hours were set, it said how many machines the gym has (for example \"12 machines\"). Now it shows the name of the gym you chose (for example \"City gym\"). The other lines are as they were: \"Today: 3 machines · 7 sets\", the open-now line, and \"Photo, weight and reps per machine\" when the gym has no machine yet.",
            "Changed: the \"End\" button on the green \"Session going\" line at the top of the gym screen is now red. Before, it was green, the same as the line, so it blended in. Now it is red (a strong red by day, a lighter red by night) and stands apart from the line.",
            "Changed: tapping \"End\" and tapping \"Finish this session\" now both ask first. Before, each ended the session at once. Now the same box says \"End this session?\" with \"Are you sure? Your sets are saved and the clock stops.\" (or, when there is no set yet, \"Are you sure? There are no sets yet, so nothing is saved.\"). It has two buttons: \"End session\" and \"Continue the session\". This covers the red \"End\" button on the green line and the big \"Finish this session\" button at the bottom of the gym screen. Nothing is ended until you tap \"End session\".",
            "Removed: the thin coloured stripe down the left edge of each machine card on the gym screen. Before, it showed the machine's muscle group in colour. Now the card has no stripe. Muscle groups are still there: you still choose a machine's group in its settings (the pencil), and History still shows your sets per muscle group.",
            "Changed: three things now share one colour, indigo. Before, the gym's name pill at the top of the gym screen was plum, while the \"At the gym\" card on Train and the \"Back to gym\" button on a machine's screen were indigo. Now all three are the same indigo.",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.26", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: a new look for the whole app, \"Cards and glass\". Nothing works differently; only the colours and shapes changed. The page background used to be grey (light #f4f6f7, dark #0e1416). Now it is a soft indigo-tinted wash: pale (#eef0fa) by day and deep (#121326) by night. Cards used to be plain white by day; they are still white by day, and at night they are a deep indigo-grey (#1d1f3a). The thin lines follow the same tint.",
            "Changed: at the gym, the gym's name pill, the hint line and the three buttons (Plan today, Repeat last visit, Save as template) now sit together in ONE rounded card at the top. Before, they were separate pieces straight on the page. Once a session is going, or a plan is set, the three buttons are hidden as before, and the card then holds only the gym's name and the hint.",
            "Changed: the three buttons are now one joined row, with the mark above the words. Before, they were separate small buttons with the mark beside the words. Repeat last visit is still full indigo. They work exactly as before.",
            "Changed: the search field \"Find a machine\" is now a rounded capsule on the card colour, without an outline. Before, it had an outline. It still shows only when a gym has more than 8 machines.",
            "Changed: the machine tiles. Before, the photo filled the whole tile and the machine's name sat on a dark band over the bottom of the photo. Now each machine is a card: the photo on top with rounded corners, and under it a light band with the name in dark, semibold letters and, small in indigo, the last time (for example \"Last: 59 kg\"). The coloured stripe for the muscle group stays on the left edge.",
            "Unchanged on the tiles: the Busy pill stays exactly where it was, at the bottom right of the photo, just above the name band. A busy machine now has an orange outline and its last-time line is orange (before: its band turned orange). A machine done today keeps its indigo tick and its indigo outline.",
            "Changed: the bar at the bottom (Train, History, Settings) is now a rounded capsule, with the tab you are on inside a pale pill of its own colour. Before, it was a flat bar across the whole width of the screen. Pages still end above it, so nothing is hidden underneath.",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.25", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the gym's name at the top of the gym screen is now a full plum-coloured pill with light letters. Before, it was pale indigo with indigo letters, like everything else on the page, so it did not stand out. It still works the same: tap it to switch gym, make a new one or rename it.",
            "New: a \"−15 s\" button on the rest after a set, beside \"+15 s\". Before, there was only a wide \"+15 s\" button. Now \"−15 s\", \"+15 s\" and \"Skip rest\" are three small buttons on one line, so the rest card is lower. \"−15 s\" never takes the rest below 5 seconds left; to stop the rest, use Skip rest.",
            "Changed: the green line at the top of the gym screen has much shorter words. Before: \"Session going · 3 machines · 7 sets\" and the clock. Now: \"7 sets\", \"1 set\", \"No sets yet\" or \"Paused\", then the running clock.",
            "New: a green \"End\" button at the right end of that same line. It does exactly what \"Finish this session\" at the bottom does: with sets, it finishes the session and opens \"Session done\"; with no set yet, it ends the session and saves nothing. Before, you had to scroll down to the Finish button. That button is still at the bottom.",
            "Unchanged: the green line under the At the gym card on Train still says \"Session going · 42 min · …\". For VoiceOver, the line on the gym screen still reads the long words (\"Session going, 3 machines, 7 sets\").",
            "Nothing else changed, and your data is as it was."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.24", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the Garmin Board link. Before, your gym sessions lived only in this app on the phone, and the Garmin Board on your Mac (your own page of Garmin numbers) knew nothing of them. Now Settings → \"Garmin Board\" opens a page. Tap \"Choose folder\" and pick the folder \"AMS Garmin\" in iCloud Drive (the folder the Board already uses) — once is enough.",
            "New: the app then keeps one small file there, \"Workout Companion sessions.json\", up to date by itself. It is written every time you finish, change or delete a session, and when you leave the app. It holds your last 60 finished sessions: date, start and end, minutes, gym, title, how it felt, notes, machines, sets, kilograms lifted, minutes on time machines and new bests, and for each machine its name, muscle group, sets, heaviest weight and a pain flag. No photos.",
            "New on the Garmin Board page: the name of the chosen folder, when the file was last written, \"Write now\" (writes it at once), \"Stop sharing\" (the app forgets the folder; the file already there stays until you delete it) and Done. If the file cannot be written, the page says so in red.",
            "New on the Mac: Garmin Board 1.10 shows a \"Gym sessions\" panel with your latest session and its machines, the change against the session before, the last 7 days against the 7 before, and your recent sessions.",
            "Data: nothing leaves the phone except this one file, into your own iCloud Drive folder. Until you choose a folder, nothing is written. Backups work as before."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.23", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed on the gym screen: Plan today, Repeat last visit and Save as template now show only before the session. Once you have opened a machine or logged a set (the green \"Session going\" line is showing) they disappear, and the hint says \"Tap the machine you'll use next.\" A plan you made before still shows as \"Today's plan\" with its Change button. After Finish they are back. Before, the three buttons stayed on screen during the whole session and took room from the machines.",
            "New on the machine screen: \"Last time\" for each set. In the box for the set you are about to do, a faint line now shows the same set from your last visit, for example \"Last time: 40 kg × 10 · hard\". Before, there was only one line for the whole machine at the top. It counts working sets only, not warm-ups, and it does not show on time machines or the first time you use a machine.",
            "New: how the set felt. Under today's sets a row \"Last set felt\" has three buttons: Easy, OK and Hard. Tap one and the word shows in that set's row; tap the same button again and it is taken away. Next time the word is in the faint \"Last time\" line. Before, the app did not know how a set felt.",
            "New: holds with a countdown, for a plank for example. A machine that logs time with both the level and the incline switched off is now a hold: you set it in seconds (steps of 5 s) instead of minutes, and \"Start countdown\" counts down with a ring, ticks in the last three seconds, saves the set by itself at zero and starts the rest. \"Stop\" saves nothing. \"Done\" still logs the hold without a countdown. Also changed: times under one minute now read \"45 s\". Before, they read \"0:45 min\".",
            "New: a \"Pain here\" button. After the first set, tap it on a machine and it turns red. Next time the machine shows a red line, \"Pain flagged last time — go easy\", and the app never suggests more weight or more reps after a pain flag; it says \"Pain last time — the same again, go easy\".",
            "New on the gym screen: move a machine to the next visit. Press and hold a machine in today's plan and choose \"Move to next visit\". It is struck through today (\"Moved to next visit\"), and the next time you are at that gym it stands first under the heading \"From last visit\". A plan made that day puts these machines first. Press and hold one and choose \"Not this time\" to drop it. It also leaves the list once you log a set on it. Before, you could only Skip today, and the machine was forgotten.",
            "Changed: the session clock pauses. After 20 minutes without a set, the clock stands still and the green line says \"Paused\" instead of \"Session going\". Your next set starts it again; the idle time beyond 20 minutes is not counted (the minutes of a set on a time machine always count). The minutes on the Finish button and the line on Train use the same clock. The time kept in History is unchanged: first set to last set.",
            "New: the session clock on the lock screen. While a session is going, the lock screen and the Dynamic Island show \"Gym session\", the running clock, the gym's name and, for example, \"3 machines · 7 sets\". It ends when you tap Finish. The rest countdown shows there as before. Before, only rests showed there.",
            "New: opening hours for each gym. Tap the gym's name at the top of the gym screen and choose \"Opening hours…\". A page shows the seven days, each Open or Closed with a from and a to time, and \"Same as Monday for every day\"; Cancel and Save are at the bottom. Under the gym's name the gym screen then says \"Open · closes 22:00\", \"Closes in 40 min\", \"Closed · opens 06:00\" or \"Closed · opens Monday 06:00\". The At the gym card on Train shows the same words.",
            "New on \"Session done\": how did it feel. Five buttons — Great, Good, OK, Tired, Rough. It is kept with the session and shown on its page and in Earlier visits. The title and notes fields were already there.",
            "New on \"Session done\": today against last visit. A section \"Against last visit\" shows Machines, Sets, Time and Lifted in all, each with the change, for example \"+2\", \"−6 min\", \"+250 kg\" or \"same\"; more is green. It is not shown on your first visit to a gym.",
            "New on \"Session done\": a \"Stretch now\" button opens a stretch list to tick off. The first time, the app makes an ordinary exercise list called \"After-gym stretch\" with six stretches (chest in a doorway, shoulder across the body, hip flexor lunge, hamstring, thigh standing, child's pose). It also shows as a tile on Train, and you can change it like any exercise list. Choose which list is used in Settings → \"Reminder and stretch\", or choose \"None\" to hide the button.",
            "New in Settings: \"Reminder and stretch\". \"Remind me after N days without the gym\" can be Off or 2 to 14 days; it starts at 4. The phone then shows \"4 days since your last gym visit\" at 10:00 that day. Cancel and Save are at the bottom.",
            "New in Settings: \"Sounds\". Choose the sound when a rest ends — Chime (as before), Bell, Beep or None; the rest alarm on a locked phone uses the same sound. Vibration can be Strong, Light or Off. Each choice plays or buzzes once when you tap it. Cancel and Save are at the bottom.",
            "New in the interval timer: a spoken countdown. The voice says \"Three, two, one\" at the end of every part; in work rounds of 20 seconds or longer it says \"Halfway\", and in work rounds of 30 seconds or longer \"Ten seconds\". The tick stays quiet while the voice counts. Switch it off in Settings → Sounds → \"Spoken countdown\".",
            "New: presets for interval workouts. When you make or change one, a \"Presets\" menu fills rounds, work and rest in one tap: Tabata (8 × 20 s / 10 s), 30 / 30, 40 / 20, 45 / 15 and Every minute (10 × 60 s / 0 s). \"Save as preset\" keeps your own under a name; \"Remove my preset\" deletes one.",
            "Changed: the session clock starts at your first machine. Before (1.20 to 1.22), the green \"Session going\" line, the clock and the Finish button came the moment the gym screen opened, so choosing the gym, planning today or repeating last visit already counted as training time. Now none of them is there until you open your first machine of the day (a machine tile, a row in today's plan, a \"From last visit\" row or a \"Done this session\" row). Go back to the gym screen and they are there, with \"no sets yet\" until your first set. The line under the At the gym card on Train follows the same rule, and so does the session's time in History.",
            "Data: everything stays on your phone as before. The gym file gains the new fields (how each set felt, pain, machines moved to the next visit, opening hours, how the session felt), and older backups still open."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.22", date: "18 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the name under the app icon is now \"Workout Companion\". Before, it was \"Workouts\". Train is still headed \"Workout Companion\". If the name is too long for the space under the icon, the iPhone may shorten it there.",
            "New: \"Done this session\" on the gym screen. While a session is going, a list sits right under the green Session going line: one row for each machine you have done sets on in this session, in the order you did them. Each row shows a number (1, 2, 3…), the machine's name and its sets, for example \"30 kg × 12, 12, 10\". Tap a row to open that machine again, to add a set or just to look. The list does not show before your first set.",
            "Changed: one button instead of two on a machine. Before, the green \"Next ›\" beside Set done (on to the next planned machine) and \"Exercise done\" at the bottom (back to the gym screen) did nearly the same. Now the green \"Next ›\" beside Set done is gone, and only the big button at the bottom is left. Before your first set it says \"Back to gym\" and logs nothing, as before. After a set it says \"Exercise done\". When today's plan still has a machine to do, \"Next: <machine name>\" shows under it and the button takes you straight to that machine. With no plan, or nothing left in it, it goes back to the gym screen. The \"Next machine\" button that appears during the rest, once you have done as many sets as last time, stays as it was.",
            "New: a running clock on the green Session going line. At its right end it counts every second, like \"0:42:15\" (hours, minutes, seconds), from the moment the gym screen opened today. The words keep the machines and sets, for example \"Session going · 3 machines · 7 sets\". The Finish button still shows the minutes, and the green line under the At the gym card on Train is unchanged."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.21", date: "16 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the workouts file is now protected like the gym log and History. If it could ever not be read, the app used to save an empty list over it at the next change and tidy away the workouts' photos. Now it never saves over a workouts file it cannot read, and it keeps every photo. The unreadable file is still kept aside in the app's folder, as before.",
            "New: a red note at the top of Train when your workouts, your gym log or your History could not be read. It says \"Your workouts could not be read\" (or \"Your gym log…\", \"Your history…\"), then \"Nothing is saved over them. Restore a backup to get them back.\" Its \"Backups\" button opens Settings → Backups.",
            "Changed: Restore is all or nothing. The backup's files and photos are first written to a waiting folder, and only when every one of them is written are they put in place. If anything goes wrong on the way, for example the phone is full, everything stays exactly as it was. Before, a failure half-way could leave a mix. As before, today's data is kept in \"Before restore <date>\" first.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.20", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the session starts when you open the gym. The green line \"Session going · 3 min · no sets yet\" now shows at the top of the gym screen, and under the At the gym card on the Train page, from the moment the gym screen opens today. The minutes count from that moment, and the session's time in History counts from it too. Before, the line appeared only after your first \"Set done\", so walking in showed nothing.",
            "New: the Finish button shows straight away. At the bottom of the gym screen it says \"Finish this session · 3 min\" from the moment you arrive. Tap it before any set and the session simply ends and nothing is saved. Before, Finish appeared only after the first set.",
            "Changed: once you have finished a session today, opening the gym again does not start a new one. As before, a second session starts with its first set.",
            "Changed: on a machine, the big button at the bottom now says \"Back to gym\" before your first set. Before (1.19) it said \"Back to machines\". After a set it still says \"Exercise done\". On the Mac, Escape does the same.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.19", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "New: you can leave a machine without logging anything. Open a machine, and before your first set the big button at the bottom now says \"Back to machines\". Tap it and you are back on the gym screen; nothing is saved and no session starts. On the Mac, Escape does the same. Before, the only way out was \"Exercise done\" (which saved nothing either, but said otherwise) or Set done. Once you have done a set, the button says \"Exercise done\" as before.",
            "Changed: short build numbers. TestFlight now shows \"1.19 (1)\" instead of a long number made of the date and time, like \"1.18 (202611051430)\".",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.18", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "New: \"Session going\" on the Train page. While a gym session is open today, the same green line as on the gym screen sits right under the At the gym card — \"Session going · 42 min · 3 machines · 7 sets\". Tap it to go back to the gym. Before, Train only said \"Today: 3 machines · 7 sets\" on the card, with no minutes and no sign the session was still open.",
            "New: the Finish button shows the minutes. At the bottom of the gym screen it now says \"Finish this session · 42 min\" instead of just \"Finish this session\", so you see how long you have trained even when you have scrolled down past the green line at the top. The minutes move on by themselves.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.17", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "New: \"Session going\". While a session is open, a green line at the top of the gym screen says so, with a dot, how many minutes it has run, and how many machines and sets so far — for example \"Session going · 42 min · 3 machines · 7 sets\". The minutes move on by themselves. It shows from your first set until you tap Finish this session.",
            "Changed: the three buttons Plan today, Repeat last visit and Save as template are smaller: the mark now sits beside the words instead of above them, and the words are a size smaller. Each button is about 45 points tall instead of 82, so the machines start higher on the screen.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.16.2", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: saving a new machine or exercise now only defines it. You stay on the gym screen and its tile is there; tap it when you want to log a set. Before, Save opened the machine at once, with Set done and \"Exercise done\", even when you only wanted to add it.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.16.1", date: "5 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the Busy pill is back at the bottom right of each machine photo, just above the name band, where you asked for it in 1.13. Version 1.16 had moved it to the top left without asking you. It works as before: tap it to mark the machine busy, tap again to take the mark away.",
            "New: a check that the Busy pill stays at the bottom right, so a later change cannot move it again by accident.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.16", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the machine tiles on the gym screen. The photo now fills the whole tile (132 points tall instead of 96), and the machine's name and its last time sit on a deep indigo band across the bottom of the photo. Before, the name and last time were written under a smaller photo. A Busy machine's band turns orange and says \"Busy — come back later\". A machine done today gets a thicker indigo edge and keeps its tick at the top right.",
            "Changed: the Busy pill moved from the bottom right to the top left of the photo, because the name band is at the bottom now. It works as before.",
            "Changed: the rest ring on a machine changes colour as the rest runs out — orange while more than half is left, yellow past the middle, green in the last fifth. Before, it was always indigo. The countdown in its middle is bigger (52 instead of 40 points) and the ring a little wider.",
            "New: a gold arrow going up beside a set that beat the same set last time — more weight, or the same weight with more reps (on an exercise without weight: more reps). Warm-ups, time machines and a first time on a machine never get one.",
            "Changed: today's sets on a machine sit on a light indigo wash, each with its tick in a filled indigo circle (amber for a warm-up). Before, a bare tick on the plain card.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.15", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the rest on the lock screen. When a rest starts — after Set done at the gym, between sets in a Sets & reps workout, or before an interval round — the countdown also shows on the iPhone's lock screen: a hand-drawn stopwatch, \"Rest · Leg press\", the time counting down, a bar filling up, and what comes next (\"Next: Set 3 · 40 kg × 10\"). You no longer need to unlock the phone to see how long is left.",
            "New: the rest in the Dynamic Island. With another app open (or the home screen), the stopwatch and the countdown sit in the black island at the top of the screen. Touch and hold it to see the machine, the next set and the bar; tap it to go back to the app.",
            "New: when the time is up it says \"Rest over\" and \"Go: Set 3 · 40 kg × 10\" until you open the app. The buzz and \"Rest over\" message from 1.8 stay as before.",
            "New: on the rest card in the app a small line \"Also on your lock screen\" tells you the countdown is out there too. Skip rest, +15 s, the next set or leaving the machine updates or removes it at once.",
            "Gym rests are indigo, workout rests blue — the same colours as in the app. Nothing is sent to Apple Health or the Apple Watch.",
            "If you do not want it: iPhone Settings → Workouts → Live Activities off.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.14", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the picture you share of a session now shows the session's first photo, wide, right under the heading — when the session has photos. The pictures of the machines stay as before.",
            "New: Undo Finish. After you tap \"Finish this session\", the \"Session done\" page has an \"Undo Finish\" button beside Done. Tap it and the session goes on as if you had never tapped Finish: the Finish button is back, the day's plan and the Busy marks come back, and the title, notes and photos you typed in stay.",
            "New: delete a session. At the bottom of any earlier session's page (from History or from Earlier visits) there is a red \"Delete this session\" button. It asks first. Then the session and all its sets are gone, and the dark Undo bar at the bottom brings it back for 10 seconds.",
            "Changed: deleting plan templates moved out of Plan today into Settings → Plan templates. There each gym's templates are listed with their machines, and a bin deletes one (Undo for 10 seconds). Plan today now only lets you use a template or save one.",
            "Changed: the History tab has a new hand-drawn icon — bars going up — instead of the heart-rate line, which looked like a pulse measurement rather than history.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.13", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the time of a session with time machines. A bike ride of 70 minutes and 50 minutes on the treadmill showed \"77 min\" instead of about 2 hours: a time set is saved when it ends, and the app counted only from the end of the first ride. Now each time set counts from when it began (saved minus its minutes), and a session is never shorter than its minutes on time machines. Sessions already logged are counted again the right way — nothing to retype.",
            "New: photos of a session. On \"Session done\" and on any earlier visit there is a Photos card: Take photo (camera) or Choose from Photos, as many as you like. Tap a photo to see it large; Remove asks first. Session photos are in your backups and in Check my data.",
            "Changed: Plan today, Repeat last visit and Save as template are now three tiles of the same size, each with its hand-drawn mark above its words — before, they were capsules that wrapped unevenly, and Save as template had no mark. Repeat last visit stays full colour. Save as template has a new bookmark mark.",
            "Changed: the Busy pill on each machine photo is smaller and sits at the bottom right of the photo, so it no longer covers the picture. It is still easy to tap.",
            "Changed: a visit with only time machines shows \"On time machines 120 min\" instead of \"Lifted 0 kg\".",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.12", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: \"Finish this session\" stayed on the gym screen after you had finished and saved the session — and any set you did afterwards was added to the session you had already closed. Now Finish closes the session: the button goes away, and it comes back only when you start a new session.",
            "Fixed: right after Finish, the session now shows straight away under \"Earlier visits\" on the gym screen. Before, the day's session was kept out of that list until the next day.",
            "New: two sessions on one day — for example one in the morning and one in the evening. After Finish the gym screen says \"Session done. Tap a machine to start a second session.\" Tap a machine and the next set starts a new session with its own time, title, notes and share picture. \"Last time\" on a machine then shows the morning's numbers.",
            "Changed: each row under \"Earlier visits\" now shows the time the session started (\"14:20 · 3 machines · 9 sets\"), so two sessions on the same day are easy to tell apart. The newest is at the top.",
            "Changed: the At the gym card on Train says \"Today: 2 sessions · 14 sets\" when you have trained twice that day.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11.3", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Changed: the heading \"Earlier visits\" on the gym screen now names the gym — for example \"Earlier visits · Basic-Fit\" — so you always know whose visits you are looking at.",
            "Changed: the date at the top of an earlier visit now has the year, and says \"today\" or \"yesterday\" when it is — for example \"Tuesday, 3 November 2026 · yesterday\". Before it was only \"Tuesday 3 November\".",
            "Fixed: tapping a visit under \"Earlier visits\" on the gym screen did nothing — the page never opened. Now it opens the visit, the same page as from History (the same fault was fixed in History in 1.5).",
            "Fixed: a machine tile's \"Last:\" line now only uses sets of the machine's own kind. A machine first logged with weights and later switched to time (like a treadmill) showed \"Last: 20 kg × 10\"; now it shows its last time (\"Last: 25 min · level 8\"), or \"New\" when it has none yet. The same for weights and reps-only exercises.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11.2", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the time of a gym session. Before, it ran from your first set until you tapped \"Finish this session\" — so a Finish tapped at home, or tapped again later, could turn a half-hour session into \"398 min\" (6 hours 38). Now each set remembers when you tapped Set done, and the time runs from the first set to the last set. A Finish tapped within 10 minutes of the last set still counts; a later one does not.",
            "Changed: a session you never finished now shows its time too (first set to last set), instead of a dash.",
            "Changed: older sessions logged before this version have no set times. If one of them claims more than 3 hours, it shows no time (a dash) instead of the wrong number, and it no longer swells the minutes in History and the statistics.",
            "New: set the time of a session yourself. Open an earlier visit (from History or Earlier visits) and tap Time — the tile now has a small pencil. Type the minutes it really took and tap Save; the visit, the share picture, History and the statistics all use your minutes. \"Use the time from my sets\" takes your own number away again. Handy for sessions from before this version whose time came out wrong.",
            "Kept: changing a set afterwards (Fix a set) keeps the time it was done.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11.1", date: "4 November 2026", items: [
            "New: the picture of a shared visit now shows each machine's photo — a small square beside its name and sets. A machine or exercise without a photo shows its hand-drawn icon instead.",
            "Changed: the photos in the picture are made small first, so a long visit with many machines still turns into a picture straight away and stays light enough to send.",
            "Kept: the picture still has the title or date, the gym, minutes, sets, kilograms lifted, every set (warm-ups marked W) and the new bests, always in the light look.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.11", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: a colour stripe on the machine tiles. Each machine tile on the gym screen has a thin stripe down its left edge in the colour of its muscle group, so you see at a glance what you are about to train. A machine with no group chosen has no stripe.",
            "New: \"Save as template\" beside \"Repeat last visit\". Repeat last visit plans today like your last visit; now you can also keep that order for good: tap \"Save as template\", type a name (for example \"Leg day\") and it is saved as a plan template for this gym — last visit's machines in their order. Saving with a name that already exists in that gym replaces the old one. You find it under \"Use a template\" in Plan today.",
            "New: warm-up sets. On a machine, a \"Warm-up\" pill sits before Set done. Tap it and the next set you log is a warm-up; it switches itself off after that one set (tap it again for another warm-up). A warm-up shows with a \"W\", stays in the visit and counts as a set in the statistics — but it never counts for New best, for records, for the chart, for \"Last:\" on the machine tile, or for the tips \"more weight\" and \"one more rep\". So a light warm-up can no longer hide your real numbers. A set can also be turned into a warm-up (or back to a normal set) afterwards.",
            "New: supersets. In a machine's settings (the pencil), \"Superset with\" pairs it with another machine of the same gym. Choosing a different machine lets the old partner go; \"None\" takes the pair apart; deleting a machine lets its partner go. On the machine's page a band \"Superset with …\" shows the partner. After Set done, as long as the partner has done fewer sets today, the app takes you straight to the partner with no rest. When both have done the same number of sets the round is over: the normal rest runs, and its Next button goes back to the partner for the next round.",
            "New: find a machine. When a gym has more than 8 machines, a search field \"Find a machine\" (a rounded capsule) appears above them. It finds by the name or by the setting text (for example \"Seat 4\"). With 8 machines or fewer there is no field.",
            "New: muscle balance. In History, a card \"Muscle balance — last 4 weeks\" shows, for each muscle group, four small bars: sets per week, the oldest week on the left, this week on the right, with the total beside them. A group with no sets in the 4 weeks says \"Not trained\", so a neglected group stands out. Machines without a group come last as \"Not chosen\". Sets are counted on the day of the visit.",
            "New: records wall. History → Records shows every machine's best ever on one page, the newest record first: the heaviest weight (with the most reps at that weight), the most reps for exercises without weight, the longest time for time machines — each with the day it was first done. Warm-ups never count.",
            "New: share a visit. On the page of an earlier visit, a share button turns the visit into a neat picture: the title or date, the gym, minutes, sets, kilograms, every machine with its sets, and the new bests. Send it to someone or save it to Photos.",
            "New: search my notes. History → Search my notes: type a word and the app finds every note you wrote on a machine after its sets (shown with its \"next time\"), every visit title and visit note, and every machine's setting text. Newest first; tap one to open that visit.",
            "New: rest per kind of exercise. Settings → Rest times sets the usual rest for heavy machines (2:00), light machines (1:30) and exercises without a machine (1:00), with Cancel and Save. In a weight machine's settings, a \"Heavy machine\" switch says which kind it is. A machine with its own rest keeps it; every other machine uses the usual rest of its kind.",
            "Changed: because of that, exercises without a machine now rest 1:00 instead of 1:30, and heavy machines 2:00, unless you change it in Rest times. A machine whose own rest you set before is not affected.",
            "New: fix a set afterwards — a long-standing wish. Open an earlier visit (from History or from Earlier visits) and tap any set: change the weight, reps or time, mark it as a warm-up, or remove it, with Cancel and Save. A machine left with no sets drops out of the visit, and a visit left with nothing goes too.",
            "Kept: everything you logged before stays as it was — no set is a warm-up, no machine is paired or heavy until you say so. Your backup files from older versions restore as before.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.10", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: plans as templates. In Plan today, once you have chosen machines, tap \"Save as template…\" and give it a name, like \"Leg day\". Each gym keeps its own templates. Next time, they are listed at the top of Plan today under \"Use a template\": tap one and today's order is filled in — then change it as you like and Save. Saving with a name that already exists in that gym replaces the old template. The small red ✕ beside a template deletes it after a question; today's plan stays.",
            "New: muscle groups are yours. Settings → Muscle groups lists them in your order. Tap one to rename it or pick another of 12 colours; \"Add a muscle group\" makes a new one (for example Glutes); drag the handles to arrange them; delete one after a question — its machines go back to \"Not chosen\" and their sets stay.",
            "Changed: the machine edit page, the statistics in History and the gym visit page use your muscle groups — your names, your colours and your order (when two groups have the same number of sets, your order decides).",
            "Changed: a deleted machine or exercise also drops out of every template; a template left empty is removed.",
            "Kept: machines you gave a muscle group in 1.9 keep it — nothing to do. Time machines without a group still count as Cardio, as long as Cardio exists.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9.3", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: drag handles in Plan today. The machines you chose are listed at the top under \"Today's order\", each with a handle on the right — drag it to move the machine up or down. The red minus takes a machine out. Below, under \"Add or take out\", tap a machine to add it at the end. \"Change\" on today's plan opens the same page, so you can adjust the order at any time during the visit.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9.2", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: \"Plan today\" opened a machine instead of the plan in a gym whose photos were taken upright (your home gym). An upright photo on a wide tile reached invisibly above the tile and caught the tap meant for Plan today. Photos now take taps only inside their own tile — this also makes \"Repeat last visit\" and the gym menu safe to tap.",
            "Fixed: when the app started without its workouts file (for example after restoring a backup without workouts), it could tidy away the gym's photos before reading the gym log. The gym log is now read first.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9.1", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "Fixed: the Train / History / Settings bar no longer covers the bottom of a page. \"Exercise done\" on a machine was hidden underneath it, and so was the last session in History.",
            "Changed: a gym visit in History is now colourful: the day and gym on an indigo card with tiles for time, sets, kilograms lifted and machines; a New best line; and a card per machine with its muscle group in colour, each set as a small chip, the plan for next time and your note.",
            "Changed: while you type, the keyboard takes the place of the bar at the bottom.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.9", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: statistics in History. A \"This week | This month\" switch over colourful tiles: sessions, minutes, exercises (one per machine per visit), sets and kilograms lifted.",
            "New: muscle groups. Each machine or exercise can have one — chest, back, shoulders, arms, legs, core or cardio — chosen in its edit page under \"Muscle group\". History shows sets per muscle group as coloured bars. Time machines without a group count as cardio; others show as \"Not chosen\" with a hint.",
            "New: warm-up and cardio in History: minutes on each time machine (treadmill, rower, bike) in the week or month, with small bars.",
            "New: streaks, records and badges. Weeks in a row, your best streak and records this month, and seven badges — First session, 10 sessions, 50 sessions, 4 weeks in a row, 1000 kg in one visit, 100 reps in one week, 60 cardio minutes in one week. Earned badges are in full colour; locked ones say how to get them.",
            "New: \"Exercise done\" — a big pill at the bottom of every machine and exercise. It takes you back to the machines, in place of the back arrow at the top left, which is gone. The green \"Next ›\" beside Set done still goes straight on to the next machine in today's plan.",
            "New: a machine's History at the bottom shows each visit's sets, the plan for next time and your note.",
            "Changed: Cancel and Save are at the bottom of every edit page, for one hand — workouts, machines, sets, next time, notes, plan today, the calendar and the icon picker. Escape is still Cancel on a keyboard.",
            "Changed: the gym screen has a large, bold \"At the gym\" heading, and says \"Tap the machine you'll use next — or plan today's order.\"",
            "Changed: new hand-drawn icons — a gym building for At the gym, a push-up for Push-ups (unless you chose another icon), and a real gear with six teeth for Settings instead of the sun.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.8", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: a rest alarm that works with the iPhone locked. When a rest ends — at the gym, in a Sets & reps workout, or before an interval round — the phone buzzes and shows \"Rest over\" with what comes next (\"Set 3 on Leg press\"), even with the screen off or another app open. The first time, the iPhone asks whether the app may send notifications: tap Allow. With the app open you hear the app's own sound as before.",
            "New: Undo. After deleting a workout, a machine or exercise, a set, or a session in History, a dark bar at the bottom says what was deleted, with an Undo button, for 10 seconds. Undo puts everything back, photos included.",
            "New: a backup reminder. When there has been no backup for 2 weeks (Back up now or the automatic backup), a note at the top of Train says so, with \"Back up\" (opens Backups) and \"Later\" (quiet for 3 days).",
            "New: the week picture in History shows 12 weeks instead of 8, with a switch between Sessions and Minutes. This week's bar is in full colour. Tap a bar to see that week's sessions under the chart (\"Week of 26 Oct\"); tap it again to close.",
            "New: Settings → \"Check my data\". It reads all your workouts, the gym log, History and every photo, and says \"All good\" — or lists in red what is wrong: a damaged file, a missing photo, or a file the app kept aside because it could not read it. It only looks; it never changes anything.",
            "Changed: behind the scenes, tests now prove that 2 years of gym visits and a backup with 200 photos stay fast (a backup of that size takes under a second), and the automatic tests on GitHub run again after every change.",
            "Fixed: since 1.6 one automatic test could no longer reach a machine's Weight step setting (the form had grown by the Icon row). Only the test was wrong; the app was fine.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.7", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: \"Repeat last visit\" on the gym screen, beside \"Plan today\". One tap plans today with the machines and exercises of your last visit to this gym, in the order you used them. Machines deleted since then are left out. It shows only when there is a last visit and no plan yet today; the plan then works as any plan — Later, Skip today, Swap, Remove, Change.",
            "New: automatic backup. Settings → Backups → \"Back up automatically…\" asks once for a folder — best a folder in iCloud Drive. The app saves a backup there straight away, then by itself once a day, when you open the app or leave it. Only the newest 7 of its backups in that folder are kept; other files there are never touched.",
            "New: the Automatic part of Backups shows the folder, when the last automatic backup was made, and a red line if one could not be saved. \"Choose another folder…\" changes the folder; \"Stop automatic backup\" turns it off (the backups already in the folder stay).",
            "Fixed: in 1.6 test builds, a second file picker on the Backups page could stay closed. One picker now serves both \"Restore from a file…\" and choosing the folder.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.6", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: exercises without a machine. The gym's add tile now says \"New machine or exercise\". Push-ups, sit-ups and pull-ups can be logged in the gym log like any machine, with reps only and no weight.",
            "New: \"Skip photo\". When the camera opens for a new machine, a \"Skip photo\" button goes straight to the form without a photo. The tile then shows the hand-drawn strength mark instead of a picture.",
            "New: \"What you log\" in the machine form has a third choice, \"Reps only\", next to Weight × reps and Time. The form is then headed \"New exercise\" (\"Edit exercise\" when you change one), and the delete button says \"Delete exercise\".",
            "New: a reps-only exercise has its own \"Rest\" setting (none up to 5:00 in 15-second steps, usual 1:30) but no weight step and no \"More weight at\", because there is no weight.",
            "New: a new reps-only exercise starts at 10 reps. On the exercise screen you only set the reps, with − and + (or type the number). The set editor and \"Next time\" ask for reps only too.",
            "New: getting stronger on an exercise. When every set last time reached the first set's reps, it suggests one rep more — for example \"Try 16 reps — every set last time reached 15\".",
            "New: \"New best\" on a reps-only exercise means the most reps in one set. The small chart in History shows reps per visit, and its axis says reps.",
            "New: reps-only exercises are written plainly. A set reads \"12 reps\", an entry \"15, 15, 12 reps\", and the tile on the gym screen shows \"Last: 15 reps\".",
            "New: Plan today, Busy, Next ›, notes, \"Next time\" and the history of earlier visits all work for exercises just as they do for machines.",
            "New: a plank. Choose Time in \"What you log\" and turn \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" off — you log only the minutes.",
            "Changed: a visit with only reps-only exercises no longer shows \"0 kg\". The \"Lifted\" tile and month line in History, the visit page and the Finish summary leave the kilograms out, and \"Lifted in all\" is hidden when nothing was lifted.",
            "New: Settings → Backups. A new row in Settings opens a page for keeping your data safe.",
            "New: \"Back up now\" (a full-colour navy button) makes ONE file, named like \"Workouts backup 2026-11-03 1530.json\", with all your workouts, the gym log, History and every photo. The iPhone's share sheet opens so you can save it to Files, iCloud Drive or send it by AirDrop. A file in iCloud Drive stays safe even if the app is deleted.",
            "New: \"Restore from a file…\" lets you pick a backup file. The app reads it first: a file that is not a Workouts backup, or is damaged, is refused and nothing is changed. Otherwise it shows the date of the backup and what it holds — for example \"3 workouts · 12 machines · 40 gym visits · 25 other sessions · 30 photos\" — and asks before going on.",
            "New: Restore replaces what is on the iPhone with the backup. Before it does, today's data is kept aside in a \"Before restore\" folder inside the app, so a wrong restore can be undone.",
            "New: \"On this iPhone\". Once a week, when the app starts, it keeps a copy of everything by itself. The newest 4 are kept and older ones go. They are listed with their date; tap one to restore it (the same question is asked first). \"Keep a copy now\" makes one at once. These copies go if the app is deleted, so keep one in Files too.",
            "Changed: machines and everything you logged before 1.6 are untouched. Your older data reads exactly as before.",
            "Fixed: each gym keeps its own plan for today. Before, the app kept one plan for all gyms, so planning a second gym wiped the first gym's plan.",
            "New: choose your own icons. On a workout's edit page, tap Icon. Touch and hold the At the gym tile and tap \"Change icon…\". A machine or exercise without a photo has an Icon row in its form. Every picker has a search, Cancel, Save and \"Use the usual icon\".",
            "Changed: \"At the gym\" on the Train tab is one size larger.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.5", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: three tabs at the bottom of the app, each with a hand-drawn mark — Train, History and Settings. Train keeps its place when you switch between tabs; History and Settings open fresh.",
            "New: the Train tab is headed \"Workout Companion\". The name under the app icon stays \"Workouts\".",
            "New: on Train, At the gym is a wide indigo tile at the top, in full colour. Your workouts are full-colour tiles in two columns, each with its icon, name, a summary and a play mark. Tap a tile to start it, tap the pencil at its top right to edit it, or touch and hold it for Edit, Duplicate and Delete.",
            "New: a dashed \"New workout\" tile after your workouts. The + at the top right still makes a new workout too.",
            "New: \"Log an earlier day…\" in the gym-name menu, for a session you forgot to log. It opens a calendar (Cancel and Done). While an earlier day is chosen, an orange bar says \"Logging for Saturday 31 October\" with \"Back to today\".",
            "New: \"On this machine\" in the machine form (weight machines only) — three settings for each machine. \"Rest after each set\": none up to 5:00 in 15-second steps (usual 1:30). \"Weight step\": 1, 2.5 or 5 kg (usual 2.5). \"More weight at\": 3 to 50 reps (usual 12).",
            "New: the weight step is used by − and + on the machine and in \"Next time\", and by the suggestion of more weight.",
            "New: when every set last time reached the \"More weight at\" number of reps, the machine suggests one step more next time, with two reps fewer — for example \"Try 45 kg — every set last time reached 10 reps\".",
            "New: with the rest set to none, Set done goes straight on to the next set, with no rest ring.",
            "Changed: History is no longer a card among your workouts. It has its own tab.",
            "Changed: Settings is a tab too, so it has no Done button, and the gear at the top left of the home screen is gone.",
            "Changed: the date at the top right of the gym screen is gone. It is always today by itself; use \"Log an earlier day…\" for another day.",
            "Changed: machines you do not change keep the usual 1:30 rest, 2.5 kg step and 12 reps, so everything works as before.",
            "New: on the gym machine screen, from the first set on, a green \"Next ›\" button sits on the same line as \"Set done\" (\"Done\" on a time machine), with the next planned machine's name in small letters under \"Next\". It takes the place of the separate \"Done with this machine\" button under the sets, and does the same job: to the next planned machine, else back to the machines.",
            "New: time machines (treadmill, rowing machine, bike) can say what they have. In the machine's edit page, \"On this machine\" has two switches, \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" (both on as usual). Turn off the level on a treadmill, or the incline on a bike: the machine screen and \"Next time\" then only ask for what the machine has, and the words leave it out — \"25 min · incline 3 %\".",
            "Changed: History is more colourful. The four \"This week\" numbers are full-colour tiles — Sessions plum, Minutes green, Lifted indigo, Weeks in a row orange — and each filter chip has its own colour: All plum, At the gym indigo, and each workout its own colour.",
            "Fixed: tapping a session in History opens it again. In 1.4 it showed an empty page with a yellow warning triangle.",
            "Changed: History and Settings open fresh each time you choose their tab. Train keeps its place, so the gym screen stays where you were.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.4", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: more than one gym. The gym's name sits at the top of the gym screen — tap it to switch gym, to make a \"New gym…\" or to \"Rename this gym…\". Each gym has its own machines and its own visits. Everything you had before is now in \"My gym\" (you can rename it). The app opens at the gym you used last.",
            "New: Plan today (you do not have to use it). Tap \"Plan today\", tap the machines in the order you want them, then Save. \"Today's plan\" lists them with numbers and shows Up next, Done, Busy or Skipped.",
            "New: touch and hold a planned machine for Later (to the end of the plan), Skip today (and Back in today's plan), Swap for… or Remove from plan. You can still tap any machine whenever you like. A busy machine is passed over, and Finish ends the plan.",
            "New: \"Done with this machine\" under the sets, from the first set on. With a plan it goes straight to the next planned machine (\"Next: Leg press\"); without one it takes you back to the machines.",
            "New: during the rest, once you have done as many sets as last time, a big \"Next machine\" button appears (with the machine's name when there is a plan).",
            "New: machines for time — treadmill, rowing machine, bike. In the machine form, \"What you log\" is Weight × reps or Time. Time logs minutes, level and incline (%), shown like \"25 min · level 8 · incline 2.5 %\". A new time machine starts at 20 min, level 5. There is no rest ring and no New best for time.",
            "New: \"How did it feel? Next time…\" after the first set. Choose next time's weight and reps (or time, level and incline) and write a note. Next time the machine starts with those numbers (\"Your plan from last time: 45 kg × 15\") and shows your note under \"Last time\". Earlier visits show them too.",
            "New: Instructions photo. In the machine form, \"Instructions\" lets you take or choose a photo of the machine's instruction plate. On the machine screen a small \"Instructions\" picture opens it full screen.",
            "New: after Finish (\"Session done\") you can give the visit a title (suggested: \"Tuesday at My gym\") and write notes. They are saved with Done. Earlier visits show the title, and the pencil on a visit changes its title and notes (Cancel and Save).",
            "New: History — a new plum card under At the gym on the home screen. It lists every gym session and every Sets & reps, Interval and Exercise-list workout you did, newest first, finished or ended early (marked \"ended early\").",
            "New: History has filter chips — All, At the gym, and one for each workout. At the top: this week (sessions, minutes, kilograms lifted, weeks in a row), a line for this month, and a bar chart of minutes per week for the last 8 weeks.",
            "New: tap a workout in History to see its details; the pencil changes its title and notes, and \"Delete from History\" removes it after asking. Tap a gym session to open the visit.",
            "Changed: \"Skip\" during a rest now says \"Skip rest\" — at the gym and in Sets & reps and Interval workouts.",
            "Changed: \"Finish\" at the gym now says \"Finish this session\".",
            "Fixed: correcting or removing a set you had already done, and saving a plan, could close the app. They no longer do.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.3", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: Busy. When someone is on a machine, tap Busy on its photo. The machine turns orange and moves up to a new row, \"Come back to\", at the top of the gym screen — so you remember it once you have done the others.",
            "New: when the machine is free, just tap it. Opening it, or doing a set on it, takes the Busy mark away by itself. A second tap on Busy also takes it away.",
            "New: Finish clears every Busy mark of the day, and a mark left from another day never comes back.",
            "Changed: the machines that are not busy are listed under \"Other machines\" while something is busy; otherwise the gym screen looks as before.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.2", date: "3 November 2026", items: [
            "New: At the gym — the card at the top of Workouts. For a gym where you use machines in whatever order they come free.",
            "New: at a new machine, the camera opens; then you give it a name and, if you like, how it is set up (\"Seat 4, handles 2\"). The date is today by itself; the date at the top changes it.",
            "New: each machine is a photo tile. Tap whichever is free. A tick shows the machines done today; the line under it says how many sets, or the weight last time.",
            "New: on a machine you see its photo (tap to enlarge), its setting, and what you did last time. Weight and reps are filled in from last time, so a set is usually one tap on Set done. − and + change the weight by 2.5 kg and the reps by 1; tap a number to type it. 0 kg means body weight.",
            "New: Set done starts a 1:30 rest with a ring, +15 s and Skip, and a beep and spoken words when the next set starts. Tap a set you did to change or remove it.",
            "New: when every set last time reached 12 reps, the machine suggests 2.5 kg more. A weight heavier than ever before shows New best.",
            "New: every machine keeps its history, with a small chart of your heaviest weight per visit.",
            "New: Finish shows what the visit came to — machines, sets, time, kilograms lifted in all, and the new bests. Earlier visits are listed under the machines.",
            "Changed: Save is now a full-colour button. With no name yet it stays blue and says \"Give it a name first\" instead of being greyed out.",
            "Fixed: two buttons had no name for the app's tests (Cancel on New workout, End workout); now they do.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1", date: "2 November 2026", items: [
            "New: Settings, from the gear at the top left of Workouts — with How it works, What's new and the version number.",
            "New: every icon is hand-drawn, from the shared AMS icon library — a kettlebell for Sets & reps, a stretching figure for Exercise lists, a stopwatch for Interval timers.",
            "New: the marks on the buttons (Done, Skip, Pause, Close, Add, Edit…) are hand-drawn too, from the same shared library.",
            "New: the app icon is a white hand-drawn stopwatch on a calm orange background.",
            "Changed: the colours are the fifteen shared AMS colours, in two rows of eight. A workout that had Light blue or Light yellow now shows orange until you pick again.",
            "Changed: Workouts, New workout and the exercise list are more compact — smaller tiles, less space between rows, standard text sizes.",
            "Changed: a new workout has Cancel as well as Save.",
            "Changed: the name under the app icon is now Workouts. It was Companion, which Apple keeps for one of its own apps.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.0", date: "2 November 2026", items: [
            "The first version: Sets & reps with a rest timer, Exercise lists with a note and a photo per exercise, and Interval timers.",
            "Sound, vibration and spoken words during a workout; the screen stays on.",
            "Three examples to start with: Push-ups, Intervals and Doctor's exercises.",
        ]),
    ]

    public static let howItWorks: [(title: String, text: String)] = [
        ("Workouts", "The app has three tabs in a rounded bar floating at the bottom: Workouts, History and Settings, the tab you are on inside a pale pill; each keeps its place when you switch. The first tab, Workouts, is headed \"Workout Companion\" (the name under the app icon is \"Workout Companion\"). Before version 1.28 this tab was called Train. At the top is the wide indigo At the gym tile. Below it, your workouts are full-colour tiles in two columns. Each tile has three taps: tap the tile itself to see the plan (a page you can read but not change, closed with Done; nothing starts there); tap the pencil at its top right to edit it; tap the round play button at its bottom right to start the workout. Touch and hold a tile for Edit, Duplicate or Delete. The round blue + at the bottom right, above the bar, makes a new one."),
        ("Sets & reps", "For one exercise in sets, like push-ups 5 × 20. During the workout you see the set and the reps in large numbers. Tap Done after each set; the rest timer starts by itself. −15 s and +15 s change the rest by 15 seconds (−15 s never goes below 5 seconds left), Skip rest ends the rest early. A finished or ended workout goes into History."),
        ("Exercise lists", "For a list of different exercises, like the ones from your doctor. Each exercise has a name, an amount (\"3 × 10\"), a note on how to do it and, if you like, a photo. During the workout, tap an exercise to tick it off; tap the photo to see it large. When every exercise is ticked, the list says Well done."),
        ("Interval timers", "Rounds of work and rest against the clock, after a 5-second Get ready. Pause stops the clock, Skip rest goes straight to the next part. A finished or ended workout goes into History. When you make or change one, the \"Presets\" menu fills rounds, work and rest in one tap: Tabata (8 × 20 s / 10 s), 30 / 30, 40 / 20, 45 / 15 and Every minute (10 × 60 s / 0 s). \"Save as preset\" keeps your own under a name and \"Remove my preset\" deletes one. The voice counts \"Three, two, one\" at the end of every part, says \"Halfway\" in work rounds of 20 s or longer and \"Ten seconds\" in work rounds of 30 s or longer (switch it off in Settings → Sounds)."),
        ("Sounds and words", "At the start of every set, round and rest the iPhone beeps, vibrates and says what comes next. The last three seconds of a countdown tick. The screen stays on while a workout runs, and the sound plays even with the ring/silent switch on. Since 1.23 you choose the sounds in Settings → Sounds: the sound when a rest ends (Chime, Bell, Beep or None, also used by the rest alarm on a locked phone), the vibration (Strong, Light or Off) and the spoken countdown in interval workouts. The tick stays quiet while the voice counts. Each choice plays once when you tap it; Cancel and Save are at the bottom."),
        ("At the gym", "The card at the top of Workouts. At the top of the gym screen one rounded card holds the gym's name, on a full indigo button as wide as the card (the same indigo as the At the gym card on Workouts and the Back to gym button; the name on the left, a down arrow on the right), the opening hours line under it, the hint line and, before the session starts, the two green tiles Plan today and Repeat last visit, equal in size (the green of the Session going line, the mark above the words). Each machine below is a card: its photo on top, and under the photo a light band with the name and, small in indigo, the last time (\"Last: 59 kg\"); a busy machine has an orange outline, and one done today keeps its tick. The gym's name button: tap it and a plate slides up from the bottom, headed \"Choose gym\". Each gym's row starts with a small square: tap it to take a photo of the gym, choose one from Photos or remove it; the photo then shows there instead of the gym mark. Each gym is a rounded row with its name on one line and, when opening hours are set, the open-now line under it; the gym you are in has an indigo outline, a green \"Here now\" label and a filled circle with a tick. Tap a gym to switch to it. Under the gyms are four buttons: \"New gym\", \"Rename this gym\", \"Opening hours\" and \"Log an earlier day\"; \"Done\" closes the plate without changing anything. Each gym has its own machines and visits; the app opens at the gym you used last. At each machine: tap \"New machine or exercise\", take a photo (or tap Skip photo if there is nothing to photograph, like push-ups), give it a name and, if you like, how it is set up — \"Seat 4, handles 2\" — then Save. You stay on the gym screen with the new tile there; tap it when you want to log a set. From the moment you open your first machine today (not the gym screen itself), a green line at the top shows your sets in short words (\"7 sets\", \"1 set\", \"No sets yet\", or \"Paused\" after 20 quiet minutes), then a running clock counting hours, minutes and seconds (\"0:42:15\"), then a red \"End\" button. It asks first, \"End this session?\", with the buttons \"End session\" and \"Continue the session\"; the big \"Finish this session\" button at the bottom asks the very same question. Once the session has a set, the box also has a red \"Discard session\": it asks \"Discard this session?\" (\"All N sets of this session are deleted. It will not show in Earlier visits or History. This cannot be undone.\"; \"Discard session\" or \"Keep the session\"), then deletes the session and its sets, stops the clock and clears that day's Busy marks and plan, with no Well done summary. After \"End session\" it does the same as \"Finish this session\" at the bottom (with sets it finishes and opens Session done; with no set it ends the session and saves nothing). Before, \"Finish this session\" finished at once; now it asks first, like End. Once you have done a set, \"Done this session\" lists right under it each machine you did, in order, with its sets (\"1  Leg press  30 kg × 12, 12, 10\"); tap a row to open that machine again. A line \"Session going · 42 min · …\" (with the minutes instead of the clock) shows under the At the gym card on Workouts (tap it to go back to the gym), and the Finish button at the bottom comes with it and carries the minutes too — \"Finish this session · 42 min\". Tap Finish before any set (after opening a machine) and the session ends and nothing is saved. Next time, tap the machine's photo; use the machines in any order, whichever is free. The day is always today by itself. Forgot to log a session? Tap the gym's name, then \"Log an earlier day\" on the plate, pick the day in the calendar and tap Done. An orange bar says \"Logging for Saturday 31 October\"; \"Back to today\" returns. Tap the gym's name and choose \"Opening hours\" on the plate to set the seven days, each Open or Closed with a from and a to time (\"Same as Monday for every day\" helps; Cancel and Save). Under the name the gym screen then says \"Open · closes 22:00\", \"Closes in 40 min\", \"Closed · opens 06:00\" or \"Closed · opens Monday 06:00\", and the At the gym card on Workouts says the same; when nothing is logged today and no hours are set, that card shows the gym's name instead. Press and hold a machine in today's plan and choose \"Move to next visit\": it is struck through today, and next time at this gym it stands first under \"From last visit\" (press and hold and choose \"Not this time\" to drop it; it also leaves once you log a set on it). If you stop for 20 minutes without a set, the green line says \"Paused\" and the clock stands still until your next set; the idle time beyond 20 minutes is not counted."),
        ("Plan today", "If you like to know what comes next: before the session starts, tap the green Plan today tile (it is hidden once you have opened a machine; a plan made before stays as Today's plan with Change), tap the machines in the order you want, then Save. Today's plan shows numbers and Up next, Done, Busy or Skipped. Touch and hold a planned machine for Later, Skip today (and Back in today's plan), Swap for… or Remove from plan. You can still tap any machine you like, busy machines are passed over, and Finish ends the plan. A machine you moved to the next visit comes first in a plan made that day."),
        ("Next machine", "On a machine there is one button at the bottom. Before your first set it says \"Back to gym\" and saves nothing; after a set it says \"Exercise done\". If today's plan has a machine still to do, \"Next: <name>\" shows under it and the button takes you straight there; without a plan, or at the end of it, it goes back to the gym screen. During the rest, once you have done as many sets as last time, a big \"Next machine\" button does the same."),
        ("Busy machines", "Someone on a machine? Tap Busy on its photo. It turns orange and moves to \"Come back to\" at the top, so you do the other machines first and do not forget it. When it is free, tap the machine — the Busy mark goes by itself. Tap Busy again to take the mark away without opening it. Finish clears every Busy mark. The Busy pill sits at the bottom right of the photo, just above the name band under it, and a busy machine gets an orange outline and its last-time line turns orange."),
        ("Logging a set", "On a machine you see what you did last time, and the weight and reps are already filled in from it. Change what is different with − and + (the machine's weight step, usually 2.5 kg, and 1 rep) or tap anywhere on the number between them to type it (the whole number is selected, so you just type the new one; comma or point both work, Done closes the keyboard); 0 kg means body weight. Set done saves the set and starts the rest — usually 1:30 (2:00 on a heavy machine, 1:00 on an exercise without a machine — see Rest times), −15 s or +15 s to change it (never below 5 seconds left), Skip rest to go on. If the machine's rest is set to none, Set done goes straight on to the next set. Tap a set you did to change or remove it. On the gym screen each machine's photo fills its tile, with its name and last time on a band along the bottom. During the rest the ring goes from orange to yellow to green as the next set comes near. Each set you did today has a tick in a circle; a gold arrow going up means that set beat the same set last time (more weight, or the same weight with more reps). In the box for the set you are about to do, a faint line shows the same set from last time (\"Last time: 40 kg × 10 · hard\"; warm-ups are not counted, and it does not show on time machines or the first time). Under today's sets, \"Last set felt\" has Easy, OK and Hard: tap one and the word shows in that set's row, tap it again to take it away. After the first set, \"Pain here\" turns red when on; next time the machine shows a red line \"Pain flagged last time — go easy\" and the app does not suggest more weight or reps (\"Pain last time — the same again, go easy\"). During the rest, a pale indigo \"Weight\" row under \"Next: set N\" lets you change the next set's weight with minus and plus (the machine's weight step; 0 reads \"Body\") or by typing it, and a \"Reps\" row under it does the same for the reps; the line follows at once. They show only on machines that log weight or reps. Tapping a set you did lets you type its reps too, and so do Weight and Reps in Next time. There is no swipe back: leave a page with the Back button at the top left or the button at the bottom, so a sliding finger never takes you away by accident. A small green pill at the top left of the machine page shows the session clock with a pulsing dot; it is grey and still while the clock is paused."),
        ("Machines for time", "For a treadmill, rowing machine or bike, choose Time under \"What you log\" in the machine form. You log minutes, level and incline (%) — \"25 min · level 8 · incline 2.5 %\". A new time machine starts at 20 min, level 5. There is no rest ring and no New best for time. In the machine's edit page, \"On this machine\" has the switches \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" (both on as usual): turn one off, say the level on a treadmill or the incline on a bike, and the machine screen and \"Next time\" only ask for what the machine has — \"25 min · incline 3 %\". A machine that logs time with both \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" switched off is a hold, like a plank: you set it in seconds (steps of 5 s). \"Start countdown\" counts down with a ring, ticks in the last three seconds, saves the set by itself at zero and starts the rest; \"Stop\" saves nothing; \"Done\" still logs it without a countdown. Times under one minute read \"45 s\"."),
        ("Exercises without a machine", "Push-ups, sit-ups or pull-ups: tap \"New machine or exercise\", then \"Skip photo\" if you have nothing to photograph (the tile shows the hand-drawn mark). Under \"What you log\" choose \"Reps only\". The form is headed \"New exercise\" and has its own Rest setting, but no weight step. A new exercise starts at 10 reps; you only set the reps. Sets read \"12 reps\", an entry \"15, 15, 12 reps\", and the tile says \"Last: 15 reps\". Plan, Busy, Next ›, notes and Next time work as for machines. A plank: choose Time and turn \"Has a level\" and \"Has an incline\" off. A visit with only exercises like these shows no \"0 kg\"."),
        ("Next time and notes", "After the first set, \"How did it feel? Next time…\" lets you choose next time's weight and reps (or time, level and incline) and write a note. Next time the machine starts with those numbers (\"Your plan from last time: 45 kg × 15\") and shows your note under \"Last time\". Earlier visits show them too. After a pain flag the plan for next time is the same again, never more."),
        ("Instructions photo", "In the machine form, \"Instructions\" takes or chooses a photo of the machine's instruction plate. On the machine screen a small \"Instructions\" picture opens it full screen."),
        ("Getting stronger", "On an exercise without weight (see Exercises without a machine), when every set last time reached the first set's reps, it suggests one rep more — \"Try 16 reps — every set last time reached 15\" — and New best means the most reps in one set. On a weight machine, when every set last time reached the machine's \"More weight at\" reps (usually 12), the machine suggests one weight step more (usually 2.5 kg) with two reps fewer — \"Try 45 kg — every set last time reached 10 reps\". A weight heavier than you ever did on that machine shows New best. Each machine shows its history and a small chart of your heaviest weight per visit (reps per visit for an exercise). Finish this session shows the whole visit: machines, sets, time, kilograms lifted and the new bests. Then you can give the visit a title (like \"Tuesday at My gym\") and notes, saved with Done; the pencil on an earlier visit changes them. The pencil on a machine changes its photo, name, setting or what it logs, or deletes it with all its sets."),
        ("History", "The History tab. Every gym session and every Sets & reps, Interval and Exercise-list workout, newest first — finished or \"ended early\". Chips filter: All (plum), At the gym (indigo), or one workout in its own colour. At the top: this week as four full-colour tiles — Sessions plum, Minutes green, Lifted indigo, Weeks in a row orange, a line for this month and a bar chart of minutes per week for the last 8 weeks. Tap a workout for its details; the pencil changes its title and notes, and \"Delete from History\" removes it after asking. Tap a gym session to open the visit. History and Settings open fresh each time you choose their tab; The Workouts tab keeps its place."),
        ("Session time", "A gym session's time runs from the moment you opened your first machine today (the green line at the top of the gym screen counts from the same moment) to your last set — each set remembers when you tapped Set done; a set on a time machine (bike, treadmill) counts from when it began, its minutes before you saved it, and a session is never shorter than its minutes on time machines. Tap \"Finish this session\" right after your last set and the minutes up to Finish count too (up to 10 minutes after the last set); a Finish tapped later, for example at home, adds nothing. Sessions from before version 1.11.2 have no set times: one that claims more than 3 hours shows a dash instead of a time. Wrong time? Open the visit, tap Time (the tile with the small pencil), type the real minutes and Save — History and the statistics count your number. \"Use the time from my sets\" goes back. The session clock (the green line, the minutes on Finish and the line on Workouts) pauses after 20 minutes without a set and shows \"Paused\"; the next set starts it again, and the idle time beyond 20 minutes is not counted (a time set's own minutes always count). The time kept in History is unchanged: first set to last set."),
        ("Earlier visits", "Under the machines on the gym screen, a folded card \"Earlier visits\" (a clock mark, a line like \"12 sessions at Basic-Fit · last Mon 16 Nov\" and an arrow) holds that gym's earlier visits, newest first. Tap the card to show or hide the list; it is closed each time you open the gym screen. Tap a visit to open it: its date at the top has the year and says \"today\" or \"yesterday\" when it is. Each machine tile shows \"Last:\" — the heaviest weight, the most reps, or the last time on a time machine — counting only sets of the machine's own kind; \"New\" when there are none yet. The feeling you chose on Session done shows on the visit's page and in this list."),
        ("Two sessions in a day", "\"Finish this session\" closes the session: the button goes away and the session moves under \"Earlier visits\" at once, with the time it started. The gym screen then says \"Session done. Tap a machine to start a second session.\" Opening the gym again that day does not start a new one; your next set — later that day, or after a break — starts a new session, with its own time, title and notes; \"Last time\" on each machine shows the earlier session. Until you tap Finish, every set that day goes into the same session. Tapped Finish by mistake? \"Session done\" has an \"Undo Finish\" button beside Done: the session goes on as before — Finish is back, the day's plan and Busy marks come back, and the title, notes and photos you typed in stay. On \"Session done\", five buttons — Great, Good, OK, Tired, Rough — say how it felt, and \"Against last visit\" compares Machines, Sets, Time and Lifted in all with your last visit (\"+2\", \"−6 min\", \"+250 kg\", \"same\"; more is green; not shown on a first visit to a gym). \"Stretch now\" opens a stretch list to tick off: the first time the app makes an exercise list \"After-gym stretch\" with six stretches, which also shows as a tile on Workouts and is yours to change. \"Stretch now\" starts the guided stretch timer (\"Timer with voice cues in your AirPods\"): for each stretch 8 seconds of Get ready, then Hold with the voice saying Halfway, Ten seconds and Three, Two, One; stretches done on each side add 5 seconds of Switch sides and a second Hold. The hold time comes from the amount (\"30 s each side\", \"60 s\", \"1 min\"; no time = 30 seconds). Pause, previous and next are on the screen, and the voice plays in AirPods, over music, even with the silent switch on; at the end it goes into History. Any exercise list with times has the same \"Start the timer\" button at the top until you tick the first exercise. Choose the list, or \"None\", in Settings → Reminder and stretch: the app's own After-gym stretch, six ready-made lists (Legs after leg day, Upper body after push and pull, Lower back and hips, Neck and shoulders, Quick 3 minutes, After cardio) with a one-line summary each, or your own exercise lists; a ready-made list becomes an exercise list under Workouts the first time it is saved. \"How to do these stretches\" there, and \"How to do the stretches\" under Stretch now, open the Stretch guide: a short how-to (hold still, no bouncing, a gentle pull and never pain, breathe, both sides), then each stretch numbered with its time, steps, \"Where you feel it\" and \"Careful\". At the left of the bottom bar a red \"Discard\" asks \"Discard this session?\" and, on \"Discard session\", deletes the session with its sets, title, notes and photos (not in Earlier visits or History, no undo); \"Keep the session\" leaves it. Below, \"Save as template\" asks for a name (\"For example: Leg day\") and keeps this session's machines, in the order you used them, as a plan template for this gym (the same name replaces the old one); afterwards it says \"Saved as template · <name>\". Find it under \"Use a template\" in Plan today."),
        ("Session photos", "On \"Session done\", and on any earlier visit (from History or Earlier visits), the Photos card takes a photo with the camera or chooses one from Photos — as many as you like. Tap a photo to see it large; Remove takes it off the session after asking. Session photos go into your backups."),
        ("Deleting a session", "At the bottom of any earlier session's page (from History or Earlier visits) the red \"Delete this session\" button removes the whole session with all its sets, after asking. Changed your mind? The Undo bar at the bottom brings it back for 10 seconds."),
        ("On this machine", "In the machine form, for weight machines, \"On this machine\" has three settings. Rest after each set: none up to 5:00 in 15-second steps (usual: the rest of its kind, see Rest times). Weight step: 1, 2.5 or 5 kg (usual 2.5); − and + on the machine and in \"Next time\" use it. More weight at: 3 to 50 reps (usual 12). Machines you do not change keep the usual numbers."),
        ("Repeat last visit", "On the gym screen, before the session starts (no machine opened yet, no set logged) and when there is no plan yet today, \"Repeat last visit\" sits beside \"Plan today\" in the card at the top; once the session is going they are hidden until you tap Finish. It plans today with the machines of your last visit to this gym, in the same order. Change it as any plan: touch and hold a machine for Later, Skip today, Swap or Remove, or tap Change. Both tiles are green and the same size. (Saving a template moved to the Well done summary after Finish, where it keeps the session you just did.)"),
        ("Automatic backup", "Settings → Backups → \"Back up automatically…\": choose a folder once, best in iCloud Drive. The app saves a backup there at once and then once a day by itself, when you open or leave it. The newest 7 stay. Backups shows the folder and the last time; \"Choose another folder…\" or \"Stop automatic backup\" change it. To restore, use \"Restore from a file…\" and pick one from that folder."),
        ("Garmin Board", "Settings → \"Garmin Board\" shares your gym sessions with the Garmin Board on your Mac. Tap \"Choose folder\" and pick the folder \"AMS Garmin\" in iCloud Drive, once. From then on the app writes one small file there, \"Workout Companion sessions.json\", every time you finish, change or delete a session and when you leave the app. It holds your last 60 finished sessions (date, times, minutes, gym, title, how it felt, notes, machines with sets, heaviest weight and pain flag, kilograms lifted, minutes on time machines, new bests) and no photos. The page shows the folder and when the file was last written; \"Write now\" writes it at once; \"Stop sharing\" forgets the folder (the file stays until you delete it); a red line says if it could not be written. Done closes the page. The Board then shows a \"Gym sessions\" panel. Without a chosen folder nothing is written, and nothing else leaves the phone."),
        ("Backups", "Settings → Backups. \"Back up now\" makes one file (\"Workouts backup 2026-11-03 1530.json\") with your workouts, gym log, History and every photo, and opens the share sheet: save it to Files or iCloud Drive, or AirDrop it. \"Restore from a file…\" lets you pick a backup. The app reads it first — a file that is not a backup, or is damaged, is refused and nothing changes — then shows its date and what it holds (\"3 workouts · 12 machines · 40 gym visits · 25 other sessions · 30 photos\") and asks. Restore replaces what is on the iPhone, after keeping today's data aside in a \"Before restore <date>\" folder in the app. Restore is all or nothing: the backup is first written to a waiting folder and only put in place when every file and photo is there, so if anything fails (for example the phone is full) everything stays as it was. If your workouts, gym log or History could not be read, a red note at the top of Workouts says so, nothing is saved over them, and its \"Backups\" button takes you here to restore one. Under \"On this iPhone\", once a week when the app starts it keeps a copy by itself (the newest 4 stay). Tap one to restore it, or tap \"Keep a copy now\". These copies go if the app is deleted, so also keep one in Files."),
        ("Icons", "Every workout, the At the gym tile and each machine or exercise without a photo can have its own hand-drawn icon. Workout: edit page → Icon. At the gym: touch and hold the tile → \"Change icon…\". Machine or exercise: its form → Icon (only while it has no photo). Search by word, tap an icon, then Save; \"Use the usual icon\" goes back."),
        ("Rest on the lock screen", "Every rest — at the gym, in Sets & reps, before an interval round — also shows on the lock screen and, with another app open, in the Dynamic Island at the top: the stopwatch, what you rest from, the countdown, a bar filling up and the next set. When the time is up it says \"Rest over\" and \"Go\" with the next set. Skip rest, −15 s, +15 s or the next set change it at once; leaving the machine or the workout removes it. The rest card in the app says \"Also on your lock screen\" while it is there. To switch it off: iPhone Settings → Workouts → Live Activities. While a gym session is going, the lock screen and the Dynamic Island also show \"Gym session\", the running clock, the gym's name and \"3 machines · 7 sets\"; it ends with Finish."),
        ("Rest alarm", "When a rest ends, the iPhone buzzes and shows \"Rest over\" with what comes next — also when it is locked or another app is open. Allow notifications when the iPhone asks the first time; if you said no, turn them on in the iPhone's Settings → Notifications → Workouts. It plays the sound chosen in Settings → Sounds. Also in Settings: \"Reminder and stretch\" — \"Remind me after N days without the gym\", Off or 2 to 14 days (4 to begin with); the phone then shows \"4 days since your last gym visit\" at 10:00 that day. Allow notifications for this too."),
        ("Undo", "Deleted something by mistake — a workout, a machine or exercise, a set, a whole gym session, a plan template, or a History session? Tap Undo in the dark bar at the bottom within 10 seconds, and everything comes back, photos too."),
        ("Backup reminder and Check my data", "After 2 weeks without a backup, Workouts shows a note: \"Back up\" opens Backups, \"Later\" waits 3 days. Settings → \"Check my data\" reads everything and says All good, or what is damaged or missing. It never changes anything."),
        ("Week picture", "In History, the bars show the last 12 weeks — switch between Sessions and Minutes. Tap a bar to list that week's sessions."),
        ("Statistics", "History starts with your numbers: switch between This week and This month. Tiles show sessions, minutes, exercises, sets and kilograms. Below: sets per muscle group, minutes on cardio machines, weeks in a row, your best streak, records this month, and badges — tap one to see how to earn it. Give each machine a muscle group in its edit page so the bars are right; the groups themselves are yours to change (see Muscle groups)."),
        ("Muscle groups", "Settings → Muscle groups. Seven come with the app: chest, back, shoulders, arms, legs, core and cardio. Tap one to rename it or choose its colour, \"Add a muscle group\" for a new one, drag the handles to change the order — the machine edit page and History follow that order. Deleting a group asks first; its machines go back to \"Not chosen\" and keep all their sets. A time machine without a group counts as Cardio while Cardio exists."),
        ("Muscle groups on the tiles", "Every machine can belong to a muscle group. Choose a machine's group in its settings (the pencil). History shows your sets per muscle group, each in its colour. Since 1.27 the machine cards on the gym screen no longer show a coloured stripe for the group."),
        ("Warm-up sets", "On a machine, tap the \"Warm-up\" pill before Set done, then log the set: it is marked \"W\". The pill switches itself off after that one set — tap it again for another warm-up. A warm-up stays in the visit and counts as a set in the statistics, but never as a New best, a record, a point on the chart, the \"Last:\" line on the tile, or a reason for \"more weight\" or \"one more rep\". To turn a set into a warm-up (or back), tap the set and use the switch; you can do this afterwards on an earlier visit too (see Fixing a set afterwards)."),
        ("Supersets", "Two machines you do in turn, one set each. In the settings of one machine (the pencil), \"Superset with\" lets you choose a partner from the same gym; \"None\" takes the pair apart. Choosing another machine lets the old partner go, and deleting a machine lets its partner go. A band \"Superset with …\" shows on the machine page. After Set done, the app goes straight to the partner with no rest, as long as the partner has done fewer sets today. When both have done the same number of sets the round is over: the rest runs as usual, and its Next button takes you back to the partner."),
        ("Finding a machine", "When a gym has more than 8 machines, a search field \"Find a machine\" appears above them. Type a part of the name or of the setting text (for example \"Seat 4\") and only matching machines are shown."),
        ("Rest times", "Settings → Rest times. The usual rest after a set depends on the kind: heavy machines (usual 2:00), light machines (1:30) and exercises without a machine (1:00). Change them with Cancel and Save. In the settings of a weight machine (the pencil), the \"Heavy machine\" switch says it is a heavy one. A machine that has its own rest keeps it; any other machine uses the usual rest of its kind."),
        ("Muscle balance and Records", "In History, the card \"Muscle balance — last 4 weeks\" shows for each muscle group four small bars — sets per week, the oldest week on the left, this week on the right — and the total. A group with no sets in 4 weeks says \"Not trained\", so a neglected group stands out; machines with no group come last as \"Not chosen\". History → Records is the records wall: every machine's best ever, newest record first — the heaviest weight (with the most reps at it), the most reps for exercises without weight, the longest time for time machines — with the day it was first done. Warm-ups never count."),
        ("Search my notes", "History → Search my notes. Type a word to find every note you wrote on a machine after its sets (shown with its \"next time\"), every visit title and note, and every machine's setting text. Newest first. Tap a result to open that visit."),
        ("Fixing a set afterwards", "Open an earlier visit — from History or from Earlier visits — and tap any set. You can change its weight, reps or time, mark it as a warm-up (or back), or remove it; Cancel and Save are at the bottom. A machine left with no sets drops out of the visit, and a visit left with nothing goes."),
        ("Sharing a visit", "On the page of an earlier visit, the share button makes a neat picture of it: the title or date, the gym, minutes, sets, kilograms, every machine with its photo (or its icon) and its sets, and the new bests. If the session has photos, its first photo sits wide right under the heading. Send it or save it to Photos."),
        ("Plan templates", "In Plan today, after choosing machines, \"Save as template…\" keeps the order under a name, for this gym only. You can also save a template from the Well done summary after Finish: it keeps that session's machines in the order you used them. Next time, tap it under \"Use a template\" at the top of Plan today to fill in today's order, change what you like, then Save. The same name replaces the old template. To delete one, go to Settings → Plan templates: each gym's templates are listed with their machines, and the bin deletes one (Undo for 10 seconds). Plan today itself only uses or saves templates. Machines you delete drop out of templates."),
        ("Exercise done and one-hand buttons", "On a machine, the big button at the bottom takes you back to the gym screen (or on to the next planned machine). Before your first set it says \"Back to gym\" and saves nothing — for when you open a machine and then decide not to use it (on the Mac, Escape does the same). After a set it says \"Exercise done\", and when today's plan has a machine still to do it shows \"Next: <name>\" under it and takes you straight there (the green \"Next ›\" beside Set done is gone since 1.22). With no plan or nothing left it goes back to the gym screen. Every edit page has Cancel and Save at the bottom, within reach of your thumb."),
        ("Changing today's plan", "Tap Plan today (or Change once there is a plan). Today's order is at the top: drag a machine by its handle to move it, or tap the red minus to take it out. Tap machines below to add them at the end. Save keeps it; Cancel leaves the plan as it was."),
        ("Making a workout", "Give it a name, pick a colour and choose its type. The numbers change with − and +. For an exercise list, Add exercise adds one; its ••• menu moves it up or down or removes it. Add photo takes a picture from your Photos. Nothing is kept until you tap Save; Cancel leaves everything as it was. Save needs a name — without one it tells you so."),
        ("Where things are kept", "Everything stays on this iPhone unless you save a backup file somewhere or choose a folder for the Garmin Board file (Settings → Garmin Board). The gym log keeps every visit in every gym, and History keeps your workouts, so you can see last time and your progress. Apple Health is not connected. The gym log also keeps how each set felt, pain flags, machines moved to the next visit, opening hours and how a session felt; older backups still open."),
    ]
}
